{"id": "4dac380e-d6ce-4eca-b38f-45493531626e", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T19:05:44.095231", "source": "user", "parent_id": "28fac424-bc56-4e9c-8447-d5136d815d68", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"The last handoff reports only a placeholder string ('simple test' / 'simple test evidence') and contains none of the deliverable content I asked for at approach_review. Per the approved plan and the bindings I fixed there, I still need the full final experiment design document with every one of sections (i) through (x), in this order and without gaps: (i) Research question and pre-registered hypotheses (H1 on computation time, H2 on numerical stability, with direction labelled as expectation rather than guarantee); (ii) Rationale for why the chosen tasks, controls and metrics actually answer the project question; (iii) Treatments & controls as a single table covering A (implicit-diff via torchopt.diff.implicit.grad [verify]), B (MetaOptimizer-style [verify]), C1 (vanilla autograd, no create_graph), C2 (autograd with create_graph=True in its documented standard form), C3 (torch.func / functorch.jacrev), and C4 (hand-rolled implicit-diff reference, labelled reference not baseline); (iv) Held-constant environment as its own section (float64 only, CPU only with an explicit preamble that GPU/torch.cuda.Event are unavailable here and that CUDA-side TorchOpt optimizations are therefore not measured, OMP/MKL_NUM_THREADS=1 + torch.set_num_threads(1) as primary with one set_num_threads(4) sensitivity repeat, taskset -c 0-3, pinned BLAS, locked version manifest, scalar outer hyperparameter, mean reduction, identical outer optimizer and identical inner solver tolerance/cap across methods); (v) Measurement protocol step-by-step — warm-up of 5 discarded rounds, R ≥ 30 timed rounds per (task, method, K) cell, the explicit stability-proxy formula for T1 rel_err(g_ref=g_method) using the closed-form ridge h